#NEXUS

[ krause2007a_fig9: Panel A, read by eye. Ceratosauria and Abelisauridae, printed just under their node points, are kept as internal labels; the source line 'Sampson et al. (1998)' is not a name. One four-way node: Abelisauridae (Abelisaurus, Indosuchus, Carnotaurus and Majungatholus, which continues the backbone). 7 tips, 1 polytomies (4 children); 2 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 6 case (census 2 extended to draw 120, seed 20261231). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=7;
    TAXLABELS
        Elaphrosaurus
        Xenotarsosaurus
        Noasaurus
        Abelisaurus
        Indosuchus
        Carnotaurus
        Majungatholus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE krause2007a_fig9 = [&R] (Elaphrosaurus,(Xenotarsosaurus,(Noasaurus,(Abelisaurus,Indosuchus,Carnotaurus,Majungatholus)Abelisauridae)))Ceratosauria;
END;
